;">NIGHTMARE ON LAKE COMO</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">We=E2=80=99re in the midst of what the kid=
s call =E2=80=9Cspooky season=E2=80=9D =E2=80=93 or, for our fellow fusty o=
ld-timers out there, =E2=80=9Cautumn=E2=80=9D. If you=E2=80=99ve been cosyi=
ng up with a few horror flicks this month, you=E2=80=99ll know nothing good=
 can come from hanging around a lake at this time of year. And so it proved=
 for Manchester United, who endured an early Halloween <a href=3D"https://a=
blink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMg=
szcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgT0wLr-a4BDJODV0NjT7ZDyJiSl5PtrJ5xu-pMe5IZy8M=
oE3cC5xgsl-tfEVTPRnaQVis1IoHXoSWDiLHj8tTVaHZM3bzet9Yz7cYHcZcLkxGC6IbH7Me_Ck=
8Lkk3CeLWmp9k0KDEcldkWvRf1FRwth_VNICWpcvhvvkdH-_qxHuyGssN1yFFnzgElrg2BpdqUO=
hXxdnMdy2U2lqsOWjPL4bPJZ2h2ja879skcM2h_Nk/4v3/mWDsiXFJSsmLId5rFCIfGw/h28/h0=
01.eUDJstUcfkRYPSknOBR3DCBB-BiWzRP86aNkwVSuzHM" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">n=
ightmare on the banks of Lake Como</a> that may have driven a stake through=
 the Michael Carrick era. Hailed as the interim anti-Amorim not so long ago=
, Carrick has overseen two wins this season, <a href=3D"https://ablink.edit=
orial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEB=
gtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgHYuXnMXQUq8U9bOS0OBrGhlee_vVv15FvYPcmsPNeVuJ5q1tDGSYes=
U2Qy07qThavsL7oI82SFScV6VT-wgpv2VsQH-cdZAHGDnMzODU6SpaJHlR0YR6bJxL5-ft956Yw=
sXqCAfiAv1Zp_9hEW_wfm7es5HgWaK4JtP9Vmm5F0Xy91b24GtSpzgODJLssouwNo5hq-gJRsuD=
QPNXAeRUQjKWW-ZWB_lwlpHfT3y59ww/4v3/mWDsiXFJSsmLId5rFCIfGw/h29/h001.uhpJxVc=
a-XSVthAKOa8IM7DEL6BkCM8KZjMSqQeIY3E" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">against Ips=
wich</a> and <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.=
Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgWhxz7BCWoK0=
bRYxECZpV7Zw16SQ4S4i_M8_tVc0CzVQ_NiF_mg7kqoz3zPxZJcOWXErUa06EYF50HRE_JmOkTB=
mp6b_r6DmMB1YKOn4cyNs-uW5h-SEy4xsPg3Jos-1FlUX6TFlMIzGyA-OLcxZT0ZHdsoKhSX4o6=
LDjOyn_7lEqmQ2pig_aFiaIarTeTKChwE3QxLoTpDVoZzz-P6mAG8s51HDQlRyDmg1oQ4pU2-Y/=
4v3/mWDsiXFJSsmLId5rFCIfGw/h30/h001._Mr_YgjUbURojWY9MnQ6OoNzS2ZNV7gwHDmT6Xs=
OJts" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">Sabah Baku</a>. Como were in Serie D when C=
arrick won Big Cup with United as a player in 2008 =E2=80=93 now, 18 years =
on, he watched the Italian upstarts dance, twirl and shimmy through the set=
 of training cones he had sent out to represent his storied club.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In the dugout, Carrick appeared frozen by =
fear. If there had been a sofa perched on the touchline, he may well have c=
rouched behind it to avoid the series of jump-scares served up by his playe=
rs. At the end, he walked over to the three United fans who had stuck aroun=
d and held up his hands, looking like a cross between Ole Gunnar Solskj=C3=
=A6r and a doomed Squid Game contestant. But somehow, things were about to =
get worse. A week after Lisandro Mart=C3=ADnez had taken aim at (or, in tru=
th, just below) United=E2=80=99s hapless hierarchy, Bruno Fernandes decided=
 to swing a little lower. Asked about his side=E2=80=99s tactics, Fernandes=
 said it was =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/s=
s/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgIF=
7GHq20lJyGc5DMu2PmEeahh4bx0qCurgnxAU5mSkzkES9pARkIxqbqarXz00Bk9MUq5vy5L486o=
_O4fTp5jISgnXN9KmabKub_AXNS5ZwAMcHGJp-566AEg-QUnS4rmJKHPQC--Fu_EjNJOD7bJdiK=
x_LlNoP8zFlt9s8XmcmaqiBWBXCqMlYY23kH9VikQ4GyK5t5pIU1ws73e2l0g52Ixbk8_x5Saqe=
k1GU8p7WsOVN4K2GIyQi6epQHfCpO/4v3/mWDsiXFJSsmLId5rFCIfGw/h31/h001._q8J-9nJx=
X_5rzQKMyWeZsEaGbdXxtE83Pegwprfo7g" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">on the manage=
r and staff to see</a>=E2=80=9D, before offering a surprisingly detailed di=
ssection of Carrick=E2=80=99s pressing techniques. Now 32, perhaps Fernande=
s is eyeing the lucrative podcast market, where former United players are b=
usy making hay by stating the obvious. Perhaps he=E2=80=99s just full of it=
. Carrick fired back with a maxim that works for horror-movie protagonists =
and lazy footballers alike: =E2=80=9CIf you don=E2=80=99t run, you ain=E2=
=80=99t going to win.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">In truth, Manchester United=E2=80=99s enti=
re post-Ferguson era feels like a worn-out horror franchise, a repetitive c=
ycle of diminishing returns that has churned through managerial victims, wh=
ile still finding new ways of scraping the barrel. United fans might have d=
ared to dream that City=E2=80=99s guilty verdict marked the end of the nigh=
tmare; instead, a new team of FFP-baiting waifs in shiny blue shirts have a=
ppeared, also led by a crafty Catalan. Carrick might not make it past Unite=
d=E2=80=99s trip to Stamford Bridge on Halloween, but could Cesc F=C3=A0bre=
gas replace him? Asked before the game, the Como head coach snapped back: =
=E2=80=9CI don=E2=80=99t think that shows enough respect to a great footbal=
ler and manager like Michael Carrick, at the helm of a wonderful Manchester=
 United side.=E2=80=9D Tone it down a bit, Cesc, it=E2=80=99s giving sarcas=
tic. Fabregas is on the bookies=E2=80=99 speculative longlist to replace Ca=
rrick, but it=E2=80=99s hard to fathom why he would take the job. At Como, =
he has total oversight of a talented team, a financial stake in the club an=
d all the perks of Italian lakeside living. It=E2=80=99s a lot to give up j=
ust to be pushed around by Jason Wilcox.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">Big Website reports that Frightfest tropes=
 Julian Nagelsmann (hipster lost in woods) and Unai Emery (vampire) are <a =
href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_X=
G18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPg_e9k7cQm_1NGDfSoeETlXjHove0=
_Bdq1cRTN0u1bLTFkfFknyl6mQszhSey4--8mhzRMTNybAkJf5fkLY3GGUTyRltvWuKqfsBbEwC=
mqPvgqt_ll4k_k0RrdFml9xl9wV01zgVXU9CNKi8SaS6WQkZMULFynDbO-uoYyYs6x921zeraEI=
XuLvbF_PsaOluMdo-PzpegtMW6YKC80nr49gCH3AClan17GFgR7_0tGg12fBQYUbU1Bg2jgVyM2=
euIp/4v3/mWDsiXFJSsmLId5rFCIfGw/h32/h001.vxdILmUCSyaFCLzV9K-1q-oAOsK_JoMmu8=
7TqoTjpco" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">the leading candidates</a>. Our person=
al pick, purely for content reasons, would be Antonio Conte, who would sure=
ly combust with rage within a week. Ultimately, will it matter? We all know=
 the big reveal by now: the real villains at Old Trafford are in the boardr=
oom, hollowing out the mistreated mega-club like an overripe pumpkin. Much =
like reading a tea-timely email packed with too-early Halloween gags, bring=
ing United back to relevance is a tortuous process that nobody has the stre=
ngth to complete. For now, the nightmare continues.</p>
